<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01EV">Corollary <span data-tag="01EV">4.4.1.8</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor between $\infty $-categories. Then $F$ is an isofibration if and only if the opposite functor $F^{\operatorname{op}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}^{\operatorname{op}}$ is an isofibration. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a data-tag="01EU" href="/tag/01EU">4.4.1.7</a>, Proposition <a data-tag="01EQ" href="/tag/01EQ">4.4.1.3</a>, and Remark <a data-tag="01CB" href="/tag/01CB">4.1.1.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
